<DocsLayout title="Opening a workspace">
  <p>A workspace is a folder on disk. MarkRust shows its file tree in the sidebar and remembers recently opened folders.</p>

  <h2>Open a folder</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> — open folder dialog</li>
    <li>Drag a folder onto the MarkRust window</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>File tree</h2>
  <p>Click any <code>.md</code> or <code>.txt</code> file to open it in a tab. Multiple documents can be open simultaneously.</p>

  <h2>Recent workspaces</h2>
  <p>When no folder is open, the sidebar lists recent workspaces stored in <code>~/.config/markrust/recent.json</code>.</p>

  <h2>External changes</h2>
  <p>If a file changes on disk while open, MarkRust detects it and offers to reload. Your in-editor changes are not overwritten without confirmation.</p>
</DocsLayout>
